    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d118">

                <pb facs="0180" n="166" sameAs="frus:frus1948v05p1/pg166"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Statement Released to the Press by the Department of
                        State on July 29, 1948</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d118-f1"/>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1948-07-29">July 29, 1948</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>An agreement under which the United States extended a credit to the Iranian
                    Government for the purchase of 10,000,000 dollars’ worth of surplus military
                    equipment and a credit not to exceed 16,000,000 dollars to cover the cost of
                    repairing, packing, and shipping this equipment to Iran was signed on July 29 by
                    Fred W. Ramsey, Foreign Liquidation Commissioner, for the United States, and by
                    Mr. Noury-Esfandiary, Minister and Chargé d’Affaires of Iran. The agreement
                    replaces a previous agreeement dated June 20, 1947, which offered the Government
                    of Iran a 25,000,000 dollar surplus-property credit.</p>
                <p>The agreement provides that the American Government will be repaid according to
                    customary FLC credit terms at an interest rate of 2⅜ percent per annum,
                    extending over 12 years.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
